course: dictionary
lesson: 3999
title: One word, many meanings: gang
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one to use. «The gang of friends built a den in the woods.» Here a gang is a group of friends who spend time together, because they are building a den and having fun.
explain: «Refusing to join a gang is allowed, and it is often the bravest choice in the group.» Here a gang is a group that might pull you into doing things you do not want to do. The words «refusing» and «bravest» are the clues: you can say no.
explain: Gang can also be a verb. «Ryan's gang calls Connor «Con-fused» at school.» When a group joins together against one person, that is called ganging up on them. Ask yourself: is this about friends, a crowd of trouble, or people working? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
fact: A gang is a group of people who spend time together, work together, or join together against someone.
fact: «A gang of friends» means a group who have fun and do things together.
fact: «A criminal gang» means a group of people who break the law, so it is a serious kind of gang.
fact: «Gang up on» means join together against one person, and it is a kind of bullying.
fact: Saying no to a gang that is hurting or teasing others is allowed, and it can be the bravest choice you make.
exercise: «The gang of friends built a den in the woods.» What does gang mean here? | A group of criminals who cause trouble | *A group of friends who spend time together | A group of workers doing a job | A single lone hunter
exercise: Ryan's gang calls Connor «Con-fused» at school, and no one stops them. What does it mean to gang up on someone? | To share a sandwich with one person | To help one person with their homework | To go home early on your own | *To join together against one person
exercise: «The gang laid new paving stones all day.» What does gang mean in this sentence? | A group of criminals who break the law | A family of birds | *A group of workers doing a job together | A group of friends at a party
test: «Refusing to join a gang is allowed.» Which meaning of gang fits best here? | A group of friends who play together at break | *A group that might push you to do wrong, and you can say no | A team of football players | A crowd of people waiting for a bus
test: Which meaning fits «a criminal gang»? | *A group of people who break the law | A team of workers building a bridge | A small family of birds | A group of happy friends at a party
exam: Connor's «best mate» Ryan says, «Let's all gang up on Sam.» What should Connor think about this? | *It is bullying, and he can say no | It means they are all going to build a den | It is a lovely game of football | It means Sam will be the team captain
